{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1510321-v20-should-visceratika-3-bond-with-the-mountain-work-on-concrete","id":1510321,"title":"V20 - Should Visceratika 3 (\"Bond with the Mountain\") Work on Concrete?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-30T22:46:00-07:00","id":1510321,"title":"V20 - Should Visceratika 3 (\"Bond with the Mountain\") Work on Concrete?","content":"I was rereading information on Gargoyles on a lark, and wanted to refamiliarize myself with one of their two Special Snowflake disciplines, Visceratika. When the three dot power (&quot;Bond with the Mountain&quot;) caught my eye.<br /> <br /> For those who forgot, Visceratika 3 lets the Gargoyle meld with stone, either to pass through them or to sleep there, ala Earth Meld.<br /> <br /> What I noticed is that while the Discipline description talks about rock/stone, and even &quot;stone walls&quot;, it says nothing either way about concrete. A detail that seems highly pertinent to Gargoyle PCs and NPCs operating in the modern nights.<br /> <br /> I would argue that concrete technically is stone, or an amalgam of earth materials (which natural stone usually also is, especially as it forms layers). Moreover, if we're to assume a Gargoyle was able to pass through a medieval castle wall, the power needed to work on the earthen mortar that held masonry stones together. Since concrete is basically just mortar, with a slightly different mix, it should be equally applicable. (For that matter, brickwork should also be &quot;meld-able&quot;, though in modern structures this is likely to not help getting through any plaster/drywall that usually lines building interiors, much less the mess of wires and supports.)<br /> <br /> The consequences of this would be obvious. Allowing Gargoyles to slip into parking garages, brutalist buildings, building foundations, and even concrete pavement if it's thick enough. (Granted, rebar supports inside concrete structures probably pose a problem.)<br /> <br /> What do you think?<br /> <br /> <br /> [EDIT: I continued reading V20's Visceratika entry. Level 5 (&quot;Flow Within the Mountain&quot;) confirms that the &quot;rock-melding&quot; ability of Visceratika works on cement and concrete. Indeed, that power talks about how the Gargoyle is meant to see the urban landscape as their own playground. (Technically, only this power mentions cement or concrete. But I don't think the intention was for the Discipline to work with these materials at one power level, but not both. If it was supposed to work that way, one would imagine the designers would have specified.)]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 05-01-2023, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-30T23:00:02-07:00","id":1510323,"title":"","content":"Well the Powers says:<br /> <b>System: </b>The player spends two blood points, and the merge takes four turns to complete. This power functions in a fashion similar to the Protean 3 power of Earth Meld, and may only be performed upon bare rock <i><b>or a similar substance.</b></i><br /> <br /> I think it is safe to say, Concrete is a similar substance<br /> Improtant to note, the &quot;old&quot; version, in the <b>Vampire Storytellers Handbook </b>have a Lvl 4. power called <b>Bond with Terra </b>and that one states: partially merge into stone <b>or cement</b><br /> <br /> So I think with a &quot;modern&quot; Gargoyle could work on concrate<br /> But older ones or the ones that were mady by the Ritual and not have Visceratika but Gargoyle Rituals that gave them Visceratika-like powers (and those later eveolved in to Visceratika)?<br /> Not really<br /> At the end of the day, the last world is the DM's word in this question, but the Visceratika power should work with Concrete in my humble opinion<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-01-2023, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-01T07:04:57-07:00","id":1510351,"title":"","content":"The Gagoyles came to be as a sort of magical watchdogs/shock troops of the then incipient medieval Tremere, so being able to merge with (if not outright flow through) not only earth, but stone and other materials that might be used in the making of fortresses and castles, for either defense of their covenants or infiltration of the strongholds of any enemy overlords seems like a sensible tactical choice for the Warlocks to have gone into back then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T06:55:11-07:00","id":1510589,"title":"","content":"Related idea: <br /> Do you think Gargoyles melding with concrete are bothered by rebar? Similar to how those who merge with the earth are bothered by roots (but apparently not small roots like grass.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T07:25:49-07:00","id":1510594,"title":"","content":"I don't know if that's the case, but I've played Gangrel, and when I used Earth Meld and got a glitch or critical failure it was because the character couldn't fuse due to an iron pipe or something else buried. Applying it to this case I think it would work on anything stone, concrete or clay, but not wood, metal or ceramics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T14:49:21-07:00","id":1510719,"title":"","content":"Concrete is basically an alloy of various materials that could broadly be considered stone. So I would allow the melding as an ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-05T08:18:32-07:00","id":1510793,"title":"","content":"Personally I merge Visceratika with Protean, and the ability to merge with stone is an extension you get after you can merge with dirt. The ability to move through terrain is a level 5 power, and it works with any material you can merge with, though you may need more blood for more difficult material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}